It is the OpenClaw plugin half of the Precedent bundle gate. The grading itself
is done by the Python core in packages/precedent (`precedent evaluate-bundle`);
this package only carries the event across the process boundary and converts
every failure of that crossing into an explicit decision.

It has no runtime dependencies. `vendor/openclaw-stub` is a development-only
stand-in for the host's `openclaw/plugin-sdk/plugin-entry` module, so that this
package type-checks and tests standalone; it is never published and never
loaded inside a real OpenClaw, which supplies the real module.
